    "def": "Resolving concurrent insert races atomically with ON CONFLICT (key) DO UPDATE, EXCLUDED pseudo-tuples, and SQL standard MERGE pipelines. Core Invariant & Mechanics: Resolving concurrent insert races atomically with ON CONFLICT (key) DO UPDATE, EXCLUDED pseudo-tuples, and SQL standard MERGE pipelines. Core Invariant: Primary keys enforce (UNIQUE ∧ NOT NULL); Foreign keys enforce ∀ child.fk ≠ NULL ⇒ ∃ parent.pk = child.fk; time-ordered keys (BIGSERIAL/UUIDv7) append monotonically to the rightmost B+Tree leaf page. Storage & Production Reality: Random UUIDv4 primary keys scatter inserts uniformly across all B+Tree leaf pages, dropping page fill-factor to ~50% and causing dirty-page write amplification; monotonic UUIDv7 (48-bit Unix ms prefix) keeps the active working set in L3/Buffer Pool. (Idempotent Writes: ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE (Upsert) & MERGE)",
