    "def": "Comparing append-version heap MVCC (PostgreSQL) against in-place clustered update + rollback segment undo logs (MySQL InnoDB & Oracle). Core Invariant & Mechanics: Comparing append-version heap MVCC (PostgreSQL) against in-place clustered update + rollback segment undo logs (MySQL InnoDB & Oracle). Core Invariant: Under Snapshot Isolation (MVCC), readers never block writers and writers never block readers; a tuple version V is visible to snapshot S iff V.xmin is committed before S and V.xmax is either invalid or uncommitted/after S. Storage & Production Reality: Long-running uncommitted transactions pin OldestXmin backward, preventing VACUUM / purge threads from reclaiming dead MVCC tuple versions and causing severe table/index bloat and transaction ID wraparound risk. (MVCC Architecture: Why Readers Never Block Writers and Writers Never Block Readers)",
