    "def": "How a bulk ingestion of 5 million rows before autovacuum ANALYZE caused the planner to pick a Nested Loop Join instead of a Hash Join, stalling CPU at 100%. Core Invariant & Mechanics: How a bulk ingestion of 5 million rows before autovacuum ANALYZE caused the planner to pick a Nested Loop Join instead of a Hash Join, stalling CPU at 100%. Core Invariant: A composite B+Tree index on (A, B, C) defines a lexicographic total order (A, then B, then C): prefixes (A), (A, B), and (A, B, C) are SARGable range intervals, while an equality predicate on A and range predicate on B stops index ordering for C. Storage & Production Reality: An Index-Only Scan skips random heap fetches entirely when all queried columns exist in the B+Tree leaf payload (INCLUDE) and the Visibility Map (VM) bit confirms every tuple on the target 8KB heap page is visible to all transactions. (Production Case Study: Anatomy of a Query Plan Flip from Stale Statistics)",
