    "def": "Dissecting a classic production outage where x NOT IN (SELECT nullable_col ...) evaluated to UNKNOWN for every row, and fixing it with NOT EXISTS. Core Invariant & Mechanics: Dissecting a classic production outage where x NOT IN (SELECT nullable_col ...) evaluated to UNKNOWN for every row, and fixing it with NOT EXISTS. Core Invariant: An INNER JOIN filters unmatched rows, whereas a LEFT OUTER JOIN preserves every left tuple by extending unmatched right attributes with NULL; placing a non-null-tolerant predicate on the right table in WHERE collapses a LEFT JOIN into an INNER JOIN. Storage & Production Reality: Hash Join builds an in-memory open-addressed hash table over the smaller build relation (falling back to Grace Hash Join disk partitions if work_mem is exceeded), whereas Merge Join streams pre-sorted B+Tree inputs in O(1) memory. (Production Case Study: How a Single NULL in NOT IN Returned Zero Rows)",
