    "def": "Why FOR NO KEY UPDATE avoids blocking child foreign-key inserts, and how FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED powers lock-free concurrent worker queues. Core Invariant & Mechanics: Why FOR NO KEY UPDATE avoids blocking child foreign-key inserts, and how FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED powers lock-free concurrent worker queues. Core Invariant: Under Snapshot Isolation (MVCC), readers never block writers and writers never block readers; a tuple version V is visible to snapshot S iff V.xmin is committed before S and V.xmax is either invalid or uncommitted/after S. Storage & Production Reality: Long-running uncommitted transactions pin OldestXmin backward, preventing VACUUM / purge threads from reclaiming dead MVCC tuple versions and causing severe table/index bloat and transaction ID wraparound risk. (Row-Level Locks: FOR UPDATE, FOR NO KEY UPDATE, FOR SHARE, NOWAIT & SKIP LOCKED)",
