    "def": "Writing bounded mutations, joining reference tables during UPDATE, and weighing tombstone soft deletes (deleted_at) against partial index bloat. Core Invariant & Mechanics: Writing bounded mutations, joining reference tables during UPDATE, and weighing tombstone soft deletes (deleted_at) against partial index bloat. Core Invariant: Primary keys enforce (UNIQUE ∧ NOT NULL); Foreign keys enforce ∀ child.fk ≠ NULL ⇒ ∃ parent.pk = child.fk; time-ordered keys (BIGSERIAL/UUIDv7) append monotonically to the rightmost B+Tree leaf page. Storage & Production Reality: Random UUIDv4 primary keys scatter inserts uniformly across all B+Tree leaf pages, dropping page fill-factor to ~50% and causing dirty-page write amplification; monotonic UUIDv7 (48-bit Unix ms prefix) keeps the active working set in L3/Buffer Pool. (Safe Mutations: UPDATE, UPDATE ... FROM, DELETE & Soft-Delete Tradeoffs)",
