    "def": "Rewriting non-SARGable anti-patterns (WHERE strftime('%Y', created_at) = '2025' or WHERE amount / 100 > 50) into range-seekable predicates. Core Invariant & Mechanics: Rewriting non-SARGable anti-patterns (WHERE strftime('%Y', created_at) = '2025' or WHERE amount / 100 > 50) into range-seekable predicates. Core Invariant: A composite B+Tree index on (A, B, C) defines a lexicographic total order (A, then B, then C): prefixes (A), (A, B), and (A, B, C) are SARGable range intervals, while an equality predicate on A and range predicate on B stops index ordering for C. Storage & Production Reality: An Index-Only Scan skips random heap fetches entirely when all queried columns exist in the B+Tree leaf payload (INCLUDE) and the Visibility Map (VM) bit confirms every tuple on the target 8KB heap page is visible to all transactions. (SARGability: Why Functions, Arithmetic & Implicit Casts on Columns Defeat Indexes)",
