    "def": "Joining a table to itself with mandatory table aliases for manager-employee lookups, pairwise event comparisons, and temporal range overlaps. Core Invariant & Mechanics: Joining a table to itself with mandatory table aliases for manager-employee lookups, pairwise event comparisons, and temporal range overlaps. Core Invariant: An INNER JOIN filters unmatched rows, whereas a LEFT OUTER JOIN preserves every left tuple by extending unmatched right attributes with NULL; placing a non-null-tolerant predicate on the right table in WHERE collapses a LEFT JOIN into an INNER JOIN. Storage & Production Reality: Hash Join builds an in-memory open-addressed hash table over the smaller build relation (falling back to Grace Hash Join disk partitions if work_mem is exceeded), whereas Merge Join streams pre-sorted B+Tree inputs in O(1) memory. (Self-Joins, Hierarchical Pairs & Non-Equi Range Joins (<, >, BETWEEN))",
