    "def": "How AccessExclusive DDL locks queue behind one long-running SELECT and then block every subsequent incoming read and write across the entire table. Core Invariant & Mechanics: How AccessExclusive DDL locks queue behind one long-running SELECT and then block every subsequent incoming read and write across the entire table. Core Invariant: Under Snapshot Isolation (MVCC), readers never block writers and writers never block readers; a tuple version V is visible to snapshot S iff V.xmin is committed before S and V.xmax is either invalid or uncommitted/after S. Storage & Production Reality: Long-running uncommitted transactions pin OldestXmin backward, preventing VACUUM / purge threads from reclaiming dead MVCC tuple versions and causing severe table/index bloat and transaction ID wraparound risk. (Table Lock Hierarchy, Intention Locks & Why ALTER TABLE Stalls Traffic)",
