    "def": "Quantifying the fundamental storage trade-off triangle: optimizing any two of Read Overhead, Update (Write) Overhead, and Memory/Space Overhead penalizes the third. Core Invariant & Mechanics: Quantifying the fundamental storage trade-off triangle: optimizing any two of Read Overhead, Update (Write) Overhead, and Memory/Space Overhead penalizes the third. Core Invariant: Strict Two-Phase Locking (SS2PL) holds all exclusive/shared locks until transaction termination to prevent cascading aborts; Key-Range (Next-Key) locks or Serializable Snapshot Isolation (rw-antidependency cycles) eliminate phantom reads and write skew. Storage & Production Reality: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED scans the B+Tree index and immediately skips rows locked by concurrent workers without blocking on the lock wait queue, enabling lock-free 50,000+ jobs/sec relational task queues. (The RUM Conjecture: B+Tree vs LSM-Tree Read, Write & Space Amplification)",
